WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.520
Speaker 1: You know, the last week or so,
I've been thinking to some degree.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:10.000
It seems as though so-called wokeness is actually
the prevailing opinion.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.130
In a way, it seems as though Wokeness is winning
in the United States.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:21.949
And Eugene Robinson from The Washington Post
wrote a really great piece yesterday called

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:27.859
Wokeness is Winning, and it makes some excellent
points backed by facts, which I'm going to

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:29.170
get to in a moment.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:36.040
But when I started to suspect that this entire
anti-woke framing and campaign and obsession

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:42.260
from the right, maybe a bit of an overplay
of the hand that they are that they are currently

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:51.629
playing was polling out of Florida that a
lot of Ron Desantis's extreme anti-woke stuff

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:59.170
could potentially backfire because by and
large a majority of the country seems to sympathize

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:03.030
with the woke perspectives, even when defined
as woke.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.830
Now there's two different things here.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.729
Okay, let me give you an analogy.

00:01:06.729 --> 00:01:14.830
When we talk about health care, you could
say the government has a duty to provide a

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:21.590
basic level of care to everybody, regardless
of ability to pay very high support for that

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.659
claim.

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:29.360
On the other hand, if you say there should
be a government takeover of your health care,

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.840
very low support for that claim.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:39.009
But when we actually dissect what do we mean
here and accurately represent what things

00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:44.090
are, we see that people generally tend to
agree more than they disagree with the left

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.270
wing perspective on health care.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:53.229
The government does have a basic duty to provide
an entry level of care at minimum to everybody.

00:01:53.229 --> 00:02:00.560
If you say to people, are you in favor of
wokeness versus if you say, do you think that

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:08.569
it's important to promote equality of opportunity
and accept people who are trans and businesses

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:10.630
should take steps to promote diversity?

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:16.030
When you ask people about those individual
issues, there is significant support for them.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.190
But then you go, Well, what about woke?

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.240
Are you woke?

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.380
Much lower level of support.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:27.510
Case in point in Eugene Robinson's piece in
The Washington Post, he talks about a survey

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:32.480
that was conducted by the Nonpartizan Reach
Research Institute, NORC, at the University

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.480
of Chicago.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.099
They do a lot of different opinion polling,
and we often cite them on the show.

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:45.010
They looked at actual so-called woke issues
and found that the woke side of the equation

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:51.030
is way more popular than you might think based
on what you see on Fox News or elsewhere on

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:58.580
the issue of, quote, accepting people who
are transgender. 56% of respondents said either

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:04.720
society has been about right or hasn't gone
far enough when it comes to accepting people

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:05.980
who are trans.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.860
The woke positions are a majority.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.959
The minority thinks that acceptance of trans
people has gone too far.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:18.380
Another example on the issue of promoting
equality between men and women.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:26.620
86% of respondents say that society is either
where it should be or hasn't gone far enough

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.150
to promote equality between men and women.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:34.049
That's a woke country by their term now, of
course.

00:03:34.049 --> 00:03:37.590
Woke as a pejorative is used to criticize
these positions.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.549
But the point here is when you ask people
about their views on issues, they very much

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:47.450
are in favor on, quote, accepting people who
are gay, lesbian or bisexual.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:55.500
The poll found that 69% of respondents believe
that society has been well calibrated on promoting

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.380
acceptance or has not gone far enough.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.680
That is very woke.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:06.140
And then lastly, on businesses taking steps
to promote racial and ethnic diversity.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:09.710
Woke beats Anti-woke 70 to 28%.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:14.590
Even when you ask about schools and universities
taking steps to promote racial and ethnic

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:20.010
diversity, again, Wokeness wins 67 to 30.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:27.660
Last aspect to this specifically about schools
in the context of banning drag shows and banning

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.780
books and all of it.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:34.990
When respondents were asked which of these
concerns you more about schools today, given

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:40.530
the choice of two statements, are you more
concerned about schools banning books and

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:48.460
censoring topics of educational importance,
or are you more concerned about are you in

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:55.130
favor of schools doing that and concerned
that inappropriate things may be taught to

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:59.060
your kids By an almost 2 to 1 margin, people
are more.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:05.460
Concerned about the banning of books and the
limiting of teaching in schools rather than,

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.020
oh, my kid might be taught something inappropriate.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.660
So there's a couple of important takeaways
from this.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:19.220
Number one, as another reminder, Reddit and
Twitter aren't real life in the sense that

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.990
ideas can be over or underrepresented in those
sphere spheres.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.949
And when you actually talk to people just
out there, you get dramatically different

00:05:27.949 --> 00:05:28.949
results.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:33.539
And number two, even the concerted effort
of how has it been a year?

00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:34.690
Has it been two years, three years?

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:39.880
It's kind of all the time where but certainly
we've seen 1 to 3 years of a concerted effort

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:44.060
to go after a lot of these same elements.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:51.530
Despite all of that, it hasn't been that effective
at actually convincing people to take so-called

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:57.370
anti-woke positions, which I would call, in
many cases, just anti-science positions.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:03.750
And so for someone like a Ron DeSantis, who's
about Florida is where woke comes to die and

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:11.910
on and on and on, it may help him in the Republican
primary in some states, not necessarily even

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:18.060
all, but it may not be super useful nationally
if he were to win the nomination.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:22.849
Ron DeSantis that is in running against the
eventual Democratic nominee, because it still

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:30.060
seems that even after a blitz of 1 to 3 years
just attacking these views and these positions,

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:37.340
most Americans actually come down on what
is often characterized as the woke position

00:06:37.340 --> 00:07:39.560
will be an interesting thing to see in 24
when it comes 

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:56.110
to strategy.

